ogles2.library/--background--                   ogles2.library/--background--

   PURPOSE
       OpenGL ES 2.0 for AmigaOS 3.x on a PiStorm with a Raspberry Pi 4
       (or CM4) running Emu68: the GLES2 functions are drawn by the Pi's
       GPU (Broadcom V3D 4.2). The API is source-compatible with AmigaOS 4's
       ogles2.library: the GLES2 functions with their standard names, and
       the agl* context calls described here.

   REQUIREMENTS
       A PiStorm with a Raspberry Pi 4B or CM4, Emu68, AmigaOS 3.x, an RTG
       system (Picasso96 or CyberGraphX) and a 32-bit RTG screen for
       windowed rendering.

   CALLING THE LIBRARY
       GettingStarted.txt (beside this file) walks through a first
       program, building, shaders, shipping and debugging.

       A program includes <proto/ogles2.h> and links the import library:
       libogles2.a (GCC) or ogles2.lib (vbcc). It calls OGLES2Open() before
       anything else; the GL functions and agl* calls then go to
       ogles2.library through its dispatch table, with the current context
       (aglMakeCurrent) passed for the program.

           #include <proto/ogles2.h>

           if (OGLES2Open()) {
               ULONG err;
               void *ctx = aglCreateContextTags2(&err, OGLES2_CCT_DEPTH, 24,
                                                 TAG_DONE);
               if (ctx) {
                   aglMakeCurrent(ctx);
                   ... GLES2 calls, aglSwapBuffers() once per frame ...
                   aglDestroyContext(ctx);
               }
               OGLES2Close();
           }

       GCC (bebbo's amiga-gcc, clib2):
           m68k-amigaos-gcc -mcrt=clib2 -m68020 -m68881 -Iinclude prog.c
               -Llib -logles2 -lm881 -o prog
       vbcc:
           vc +aos68k -cpu=68020 -fpu=68881 -Iinclude prog.c lib/ogles2.lib
               -lamiga -lm881 -o prog

       With clib2 and -m68881, link maths with -lm881, not -lm.

       The current context of <proto/ogles2.h>'s calls belongs to the
       program (one per import library). A program that renders from a
       second task calls that task's functions through OGLES2Dispatch with
       the context as first argument (see <libraries/ogles2_dispatch.h>).

   WHERE THE LIBRARY IS FOUND
       OGLES2Open() opens the installed library (in memory, or LIBS:),
       else PROGDIR:libs/ogles2.library, else PROGDIR:ogles2.library. A
       program may therefore bring the library in its own drawer for
       systems where it is not installed; see OGLES2Open().

   EXTENSIONS
       GL_EXTENSIONS lists: OES_element_index_uint,
       OES_compressed_ETC1_RGB8_texture, EXT_texture_format_BGRA8888,
       OES_mapbuffer, EXT_blend_minmax, OES_draw_elements_base_vertex,
       OES_rgb8_rgba8, OES_packed_depth_stencil, OES_fbo_render_mipmap,
       EXT_discard_framebuffer, OES_texture_npot, EXT_read_format_bgra,
       EXT_texture_filter_anisotropic, EXT_texture_lod_bias,
       SGIS_texture_lod, ARB_texture_mirror_clamp_to_edge,
       OES_standard_derivatives, OES_get_program_binary, OES_texture_float,
       OES_texture_half_float, OES_texture_half_float_linear,
       OES_depth_texture, ARB_texture_rectangle, EXT_debug_marker,
       EXT_texture_compression_dxt1, EXT_texture_compression_s3tc,
       ANGLE_texture_compression_dxt3, ANGLE_texture_compression_dxt5,
       EXT_clip_control, EXT_draw_buffers, NV_fbo_color_attachments,
       OES_required_internalformat, EXT_color_buffer_half_float.

       EXT_color_buffer_half_float: half-float RGBA textures
       (OES_texture_half_float) and GL_RGBA16F_EXT, GL_RGB16F_EXT,
       GL_RG16F_EXT and GL_R16F_EXT renderbuffers are colour attachments;
       what is drawn into them keeps values outside [0, 1], blended as
       floats. With EXT_draw_buffers they mix with 8-bit targets in one
       framebuffer. Half-float RGB and 32-bit float textures are not
       colour-renderable.

       Their functions are reached through <proto/ogles2.h> by name, or
       through aglGetProcAddress(). AmigaOS 4's extras glPolygonMode,
       glProvokingVertex and glGetBufferParameterivOES are there too, and
       GLES 3.0's glDrawRangeElements through aglGetProcAddress().
       Enumerants missing from <GLES2/gl2ext.h> are in
       <libraries/ogles2.h>.

   COPIES
       glCopyTexImage2D and glCopyTexSubImage2D are drawn by the GPU into
       RGBA, RGB, RGB565, RGBA4 and RGB5_A1 levels, from the screen and from
       framebuffer objects: a 640x480 copy costs about 2.6 ms a frame on an
       A1200 (through the CPU, 23 ms). A copy from the screen still renders
       the frame so far and waits for it. LUMINANCE, ALPHA and
       LUMINANCE_ALPHA levels, and copies from a cube face or a mip level
       of an object, go through the CPU.

   LIMITS
       Textures and framebuffers up to 4096 x 4096; 16 vertex attributes.
       glGetIntegerv answers the rest.

   ENVIRONMENT
       OGLES2/LogFile  the log's file (default T:ogles2.log). OGLES2Log
                       (C/) writes the buffered log while a program runs.
       OGLES2/MSAA     4 or 0: 4x multisampling for contexts created
                       without OGLES2_CCT_PISTORM_MSAA.

   CONFORMANCE
       The Khronos dEQP-GLES2 must-pass list (17,165 cases) on an A1200:
       all pass except the documented deviation below (seamless cube map
       filtering), and timing and quality warnings. See --deviations--.

   AUTHORS
       Developed by R-Typer and Ladislawv, with Claude Opus 5.5
       (Anthropic's AI assistant). Built on PiStorm3D's V3D backend by
       Steffen "MagicSN" Haeuser and Mesa's V3D compiler; the ReadMe has
       the full credits.

ogles2.library/--shaders--                         ogles2.library/--shaders--

   PROGRAMS AND BINARIES
       The GPU runs machine code that Mesa's V3D compiler produces. The
       compiler ships as a separate program, v3dglslc (19 MB), which the
       library starts as a server when it first needs it. glLinkProgram
       looks for a program's binary in this order:

       1. in memory (a program linked before in this session);
       2. PROGDIR:shaders/<hash>.v3dp, then PROGDIR:<hash>.v3dp: a binary
          the program ships in a shaders/ drawer beside itself, or beside
          itself;
       3. OGLES2Cache:<hash>.v3dp (when that assign exists), else
          T:<hash>.v3dp: binaries compiled before;
       4. the compiler, if found: LIBS:v3dglslc, else PROGDIR:libs/v3dglslc,
          else PROGDIR:v3dglslc. It compiles the program into the cache of
          step 3 (about 0.2 s per program; its first start takes about a
          second);
       5. otherwise the link fails: the info log names the program's hash,
          and both sources are appended to T:ogles2_missing_shaders.txt.

       <hash> is the first 24 hexadecimal digits of the BLAKE3 hash of the
       two sources, byte for byte; attribute bindings are not part of it.
       So a program can ship its binaries and run without the compiler:
       compile them on a PC with the offline compiler (the source
       distribution's tools/v3dglslc, v3dp/split_shaders.py and
       v3dp/v3dp_hashname.py name them), or run the program once with the
       compiler installed and take the files from OGLES2Cache:. Any change
       to a shader's text, a space included, gives another hash.

       glCompileShader compiles in the compiler's front end and reports
       real errors when the compiler is there; without it, it only records
       the source and reports success, and the link decides. A shader
       compiled once leaves a record, <hash>.v3ds, in the cache: next time
       it answers for the shader without starting the compiler. A program
       that ships its binaries and runs where a compiler may be installed
       should ship these records too, in the same shaders/ drawer:
       glCompileShader looks in PROGDIR:shaders/, then in the cache. Take
       them from OGLES2Cache: with the binaries, or write them on a PC with
       the source distribution's v3dp/v3ds_record.py.

       glGetProgramBinaryOES returns the .v3dp file
       (GL_PROGRAM_BINARY_V3DP_PISTORM); glProgramBinaryOES takes one.

   CACHE
       Make a drawer and assign OGLES2Cache: to it (the installer offers
       this) to keep compiled programs across reboots; without it they go
       to T:, and are compiled again after the next reboot.

ogles2.library/--deviations--                   ogles2.library/--deviations--

   Where ogles2.library differs from the GLES 2.0 specification or from
   AmigaOS 4's ogles2.library:

   - Cube maps are always filtered seamlessly across face edges (the
     hardware does this, as GLES 3 requires); GLES 2 filters each face
     alone. 25 dEQP-GLES2 cube map cases fail for this reason.
   - EXT_draw_buffers: a program that writes gl_FragColor draws into the
     first render target only (the extension writes it to every one).
   - A half-float colour buffer (EXT_color_buffer_half_float) is read by
     glReadPixels as GL_RGBA, GL_UNSIGNED_BYTE only, clamped to [0, 1];
     sample it as a texture to see its values.
   - glPolygonMode takes GL_FRONT_AND_BACK only: the hardware has one mode
     for both faces.
   - Framebuffer objects are not multisampled; only the default
     framebuffer is (OGLES2_CCT_PISTORM_MSAA).
   - Textures of 32-bit float formats are sampled with nearest filtering.
   - Without the compiler, glCompileShader cannot check a shader: it
     reports GL_COMPILE_STATUS TRUE, and errors appear at link time.
   - Context tags accepted but not acted on: OGLES2_CCT_RESIZE_VIEWPORT,
     OGLES2_CCT_SHADER_COMPAT_PATCH, OGLES2_CCT_SINGLE_GET_ERROR_MODE,
     OGLES2_CCT_DETECT_UNINITIALIZED_GLSL_VARS and the three SPIRV tags
     (each is logged once). The tag VALUES differ from AmigaOS 4's: the
     names are the same, so source compiles unchanged, but binaries do
     not mix.

ogles2.library/OGLES2Open                           ogles2.library/OGLES2Open

   NAME
       OGLES2Open -- open ogles2.library for this program (import library)

   SYNOPSIS
       success = OGLES2Open()

       BOOL OGLES2Open(void);

   FUNCTION
       Opens ogles2.library and fetches its dispatch table. It tries, in
       order, and takes the first that opens, is at least version
       OGLES2_VERSION (default 1) and has this import library's dispatch
       ABI:
           ogles2.library            (in memory, or LIBS:)
           PROGDIR:libs/ogles2.library
           PROGDIR:ogles2.library
       One that is too old or of another ABI is closed and the next one
       tried, so a program may bring a newer library than the system has.
       AmigaOS keeps one ogles2.library in memory, and an OpenLibrary of
       any path returns that one; so OGLES2Open expunges one that would not
       do before it tries the next file, if no other program has it open.
       While another program uses an older one, it cannot be replaced, and
       OGLES2Open fails.
       Calling it again after success does nothing and returns TRUE.

   RESULT
       success - TRUE if the library is open. FALSE: none of the three was
                 found or usable; no other function may be called then.

   NOTES
       Sets OGLES2Base. Define OGLES2_VERSION on the compile line to require
       a newer library.

   SEE ALSO
       OGLES2Close()

ogles2.library/OGLES2Close                         ogles2.library/OGLES2Close

   NAME
       OGLES2Close -- close ogles2.library (import library)

   SYNOPSIS
       OGLES2Close()

       void OGLES2Close(void);

   FUNCTION
       Closes the library opened by OGLES2Open(). Safe to call when it was
       not opened. Destroy the program's contexts first.

   SEE ALSO
       OGLES2Open()

ogles2.library/aglCreateContext2               ogles2.library/aglCreateContext2

   NAME
       aglCreateContext2 -- create a rendering context
       aglCreateContextTags2 -- varargs stub

   SYNOPSIS
       context = aglCreateContext2(errcode, tags)

       void *aglCreateContext2(ULONG *errcode, struct TagItem *tags);

       context = aglCreateContextTags2(errcode, tag1, ...)

       void *aglCreateContextTags2(ULONG *errcode, ULONG tag1, ...);

   FUNCTION
       Creates a GLES2 context and its default framebuffer. Where it draws:
           OGLES2_CCT_WINDOW (struct Window *): into the program's window;
               each aglSwapBuffers() copies the frame into the window's
               inner area. The window should be on a 32-bit RTG screen.
               A borderless window at 0,0 of its screen's size, on a
               32-bit custom screen that is not public, is drawn into
               directly, without the copy, as a full screen
               (ENV:OGLES2/WindowCopy 1: the copy always). Close the
               window only after aglDestroyContext().
           OGLES2_CCT_MODEID (ULONG): a full screen of its own in this
               display mode (OGLES2_CCT_CONTEXT_FOR_MODEID is the same),
               with a backdrop window for input
               (OGLES2_CCT_PISTORM_GET_WINDOW).
           OGLES2_CCT_BITMAP (struct BitMap *): into the program's bitmap.
           none of these: a window of its own on the default public screen,
               640 x 480 or OGLES2_CCT_PISTORM_WIDTH/_HEIGHT. That window
               has no close gadget and no IDCMP.

       Other tags:
           OGLES2_CCT_DEPTH (ULONG): depth bits, 0 (default: none); 1 to
               16 give a 16-bit depth buffer, more a 32-bit float one.
           OGLES2_CCT_STENCIL (ULONG): stencil bits, 0 (default: none);
               any other value gives 8 stencil and 24 depth bits.
           OGLES2_CCT_VSYNC (BOOL): aglSwapBuffers() waits for the
               vertical blank.
           OGLES2_CCT_SHARE_WITH (void *): share textures, buffers, shaders,
               programs and renderbuffers with this context's group. The
               group's contexts may be used from several tasks.
           OGLES2_CCT_DEBUG_SHADER_LOG (BOOL): link logs describe each
               compiled variant (instructions, threads, spills).
           OGLES2_CCT_PISTORM_MSAA (ULONG): 0 or 4 samples per pixel for
               the default framebuffer; without the tag, ENV:OGLES2/MSAA.
           OGLES2_CCT_GET_WIDTH, OGLES2_CCT_GET_HEIGHT (ULONG *): receive
               the surface size.
           OGLES2_CCT_PISTORM_GET_WINDOW (struct Window **): receives the
               window that gets input (yours, ogles2's own, or the
               fullscreen backdrop window); NULL for a bitmap.

       The viewport and scissor start at the surface's size.

   INPUTS
       errcode - where to store an OGLES2_CCE_* code, or NULL.
       tags    - tag list, see above and <libraries/ogles2.h>.

   RESULT
       context - the new context, or NULL; *errcode says why:
           OGLES2_CCE_NOMEM, OGLES2_CCE_NO_GPU (no usable V3D),
           OGLES2_CCE_BAD_TAGS, OGLES2_CCE_NO_DISPLAY (the window, screen
           or bitmap is unusable, e.g. not 32-bit), OGLES2_CCE_UNSUPPORTED.

   NOTES
       aglCreateContext() and aglCreateContextTags() (AmigaOS 4's
       deprecated names) are macros for these.

   SEE ALSO
       aglDestroyContext(), aglMakeCurrent(), aglSetParams2(),
       <libraries/ogles2.h>

ogles2.library/aglDestroyContext               ogles2.library/aglDestroyContext

   NAME
       aglDestroyContext -- free a context

   SYNOPSIS
       aglDestroyContext(context)

       void aglDestroyContext(void *context);

   FUNCTION
       Waits for the context's GPU work, then frees it and everything it
       owns. Objects shared with other contexts stay while one of them
       remains. A window or bitmap of the program's own stays open; a
       window or screen ogles2 opened is closed. If it was the current
       context, there is no current context afterwards.

   SEE ALSO
       aglCreateContext2()

ogles2.library/aglMakeCurrent                     ogles2.library/aglMakeCurrent

   NAME
       aglMakeCurrent -- choose the context GL calls go to

   SYNOPSIS
       aglMakeCurrent(context)

       void aglMakeCurrent(void *context);

   FUNCTION
       Makes context the one that <proto/ogles2.h>'s GL calls and
       aglSwapBuffers() use, for this program.

   SEE ALSO
       aglCreateContext2()

ogles2.library/aglSwapBuffers                     ogles2.library/aglSwapBuffers

   NAME
       aglSwapBuffers -- show the frame drawn

   SYNOPSIS
       aglSwapBuffers()

       void aglSwapBuffers(void);

   FUNCTION
       Ends the current context's frame: the GPU renders it, and it is
       shown in the window, on the screen or in the bitmap. The CPU goes on
       with the next frame while the GPU renders this one. With
       OGLES2_CCT_VSYNC, waits for the vertical blank first.

   SEE ALSO
       aglSetParams2()

ogles2.library/aglSetParams2                       ogles2.library/aglSetParams2

   NAME
       aglSetParams2 -- change or query the current context
       aglSetParamsTags2 -- varargs stub

   SYNOPSIS
       aglSetParams2(tags)

       void aglSetParams2(struct TagItem *tags);

       aglSetParamsTags2(tag1, ...)

       void aglSetParamsTags2(ULONG tag1, ...);

   FUNCTION
       Tags:
           OGLES2_CCT_WINDOW (struct Window *): a context created with
               OGLES2_CCT_WINDOW renders into this window from the next
               frame: another window, or the same one after IDCMP_NEWSIZE.
               The default framebuffer takes the window's inner size; the
               viewport and scissor stay as the program set them.
           OGLES2_CCT_VSYNC (BOOL): wait for the vertical blank or not.
           OGLES2_CCT_GET_WIDTH, OGLES2_CCT_GET_HEIGHT (ULONG *): receive
               the surface size.
           OGLES2_CCT_PISTORM_GET_WINDOW (struct Window **): see
               aglCreateContext2().

   EXAMPLE
       After IDCMP_NEWSIZE:
           aglSetParamsTags2(OGLES2_CCT_WINDOW, (ULONG)win,
                             OGLES2_CCT_GET_WIDTH, (ULONG)&w,
                             OGLES2_CCT_GET_HEIGHT, (ULONG)&h, TAG_DONE);
           glViewport(0, 0, w, h);

   NOTES
       aglSetParams() and aglSetParamsTags() are macros for these.

   SEE ALSO
       aglCreateContext2(), aglSetBitmap()

ogles2.library/aglSetBitmap                         ogles2.library/aglSetBitmap

   NAME
       aglSetBitmap -- render into another bitmap

   SYNOPSIS
       aglSetBitmap(bitmap)

       void aglSetBitmap(struct BitMap *bitmap);

   FUNCTION
       For a context created with OGLES2_CCT_BITMAP: the open frame is
       rendered into the old bitmap, then the context renders into the new
       one, its default framebuffer resized to it. The viewport and
       scissor stay as the program set them.

   SEE ALSO
       aglCreateContext2()

ogles2.library/aglGetProcAddress             ogles2.library/aglGetProcAddress

   NAME
       aglGetProcAddress -- a GL function by name (import library)

   SYNOPSIS
       function = aglGetProcAddress(name)

       void *aglGetProcAddress(const char *name);

   FUNCTION
       Returns a function that calls the named GL entry point with the
       current context, for code that loads GL functions by name (SDL,
       gl4es). It does not call the library.

   RESULT
       function - the function, or NULL for an unknown name.
